published_paths_modified: true (one path, named in STATE)

STATE: the source tree carries no version control at all, so `source_dirty` is true in the
sense that nothing about it is pinned: there is no revision under which the tree was
committed, and files were edited on the execution box and copied back between sessions.
`published_paths_modified` is true for exactly one path: `numbers.md`, whose scope line was
rewritten for this deposit (the lab tree's `~/research/qlora-sleep/` prefix replaced by
this deposit's root, and the rows that cite artefacts outside the deposit named). Every
other published file is the lab tree's own bytes at the snapshot time above — `paper.md`
is byte-identical to `~/research/qlora-sleep/paper/paper.md`.

SUBSET: this deposit carries the code the runs executed — `src/`, `scripts/`, `configs/`,
`tests/`, `data/` and `pyproject.toml`, under `code/` — plus the cited run data under
`runs/` and `boxlogs/`. It is not the lab tree's whole content: the probe scripts the
work used before the package existed (the `.probe_*.py` and `.diag_*.py` files at the tree
root, some of them root-owned from container runs), the container and HF caches under
`.cache/`, and the dream caches (`*.pt`) are outside it. See the README's "Not included,
by design".
